  <item>
    <title>023 由一出差就便秘想到的</title>
    <link>https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episode/64ded30280c9ec4c5f9609db</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">64ded30280c9ec4c5f9609db</guid>
    <pubDate>Fri, 18 Aug 2023 13:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><span>重要提示‼️</span></p><span></span><p><span>看题目就应该能知道，不要在吃饭时收听本期节目‼️</span></p><span></span><p><span>是的，本周一连三个差，每天不是在出差，就是在出差的路上。想起以前出差的时候，每次都会便秘，后来好像慢慢有所缓解。所以想今天聊聊到底为什么一出差就便秘，以及由一出差就便秘，我想到了什么。</span></p><span></span><p><span>【主播】山山（@山山要靠海）</span></p><span></span><p><span>【内容提要】</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="78">01:18</a> 为什么不在自己家上厕所就会便秘啊？（如厕焦虑症）</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="289">04:49</a> 当我们人格越来越完整的时候，对空间的完整性需求也越来越高。</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="389">06:29</a> 我们所需要的物理空间</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="419">06:59</a> 电影《芭比》中对空间需求的反讽</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="558">09:18</a> 我和前男友有关于“家”的讨论</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="737">12:17</a> 个人空间所代指的人际空间</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1123">18:43</a> 怎样做可以维持稳定的个人空间？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1532">25:32</a> 回到最初的问题：怎样解决“一出差就便秘”？</span></p><span></span><p><span>【节目配乐】</span></p><span></span><p><span>Jay-Lounge - Puddles</span></p><span></span><p><span>Jim Reeves - Welcome To My World</span></p><span></span><p><span>【相关文献】</span></p><span></span><p><span>Graziano, M. (2017). </span><em><span>The spaces between us: a story of neuroscience, evolution, and human nature</span></em><span>. Oxford University Press.</span></p><span></span><p><span>DOUGLAS, M. (1991). The Idea of a Home: A Kind of Space. Social Research, 58(1), 287–307.</span></p>]]></description>
    <enclosure url="https://media.xyzcdn.net/ljLI1njeD9FGafliAsHZ6T9oqZ2b.m4a" length="40256561" type="audio/mp4"/>
    <itunes:duration>00:27:44</itunes:duration>
    <itunes:image href="https://bts-image.xyzcdn.net/aHR0cHM6Ly9pbWFnZS54eXpjZG4ubmV0L0ZtMEdHbWhDdEdtYjRQbV9lNEh1ajRWbXhXMDQucG5n.png"/>
    <itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>022 「认真的拒绝」比「敷衍的讨好」更有价值</title>
    <link>https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episode/64d48bbd80c9ec4c5fe084ab</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">64d48bbd80c9ec4c5fe084ab</guid>
    <pubDate>Fri, 11 Aug 2023 13:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><span>如果让我总结今年上半年我自己最满意的改变，那应该就是我学会了「拒绝」。在过去的很多年中，我都曾备受「不会拒绝」的困扰。而我身边的很多人，也都和我有一样的感受——我们为什么要学会拒绝？又该如何拒绝？</span></p><span></span><p><span>以上就是你即将在今天的节目当中听到的内容。</span></p><span></span><p><span>【主播】山山（@山山要靠海）</span></p><span></span><p><span>【内容提要】</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="282">04:42</a> 为什么拒绝对我们来说是一件为难的事情。拒绝别人的时候，我们究竟在做什么？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="723">12:03</a> 为什么感到痛苦我们仍然需要学会拒绝？</span></p><span></span><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- <a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="766">12:46</a> 概念一：过度同理心</span></p><span></span><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- &nbsp;<a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1090">18:10</a> 怎样理解「过度同理心」与「学会拒绝」</span></p><span></span><p><span>之间的关系</span></p><span></span><p><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- <a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1148">19:08</a> 概念二：个人边界</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1414">23:34</a> 如何坚定而礼貌的拒绝别人？</span></p><span></span><p><span>【节目配乐】</span></p><span></span><p><span>片头曲：Jay-Lounge - Puddles</span></p><span></span><p><span>片尾曲：金培达 - A Story in Macau</span></p><span></span><p><span>【相关资料及文献】</span></p><span></span><p><span>有关同理心：<a data-url="https://greatergood.berkeley.edu/article/item/how_to_avoid_the_empathy_trap" href="https://greatergood.berkeley.edu/article/item/how_to_avoid_the_empathy_trap">greatergood.berkeley.edu</a></span></p><span></span><p><span>有关个人边界及过度同理心之间的关系：</span></p><span></span><p><span><a data-url="https://lovefulmind.com/posts/setting-boundaries-in-a-relationship-as-a-highly-empathetic-person" href="https://lovefulmind.com/posts/setting-boundaries-in-a-relationship-as-a-highly-empathetic-person">lovefulmind.com</a></span></p>]]></description>
    <enclosure url="https://media.xyzcdn.net/lh7vGjzZVo7EIZddnWb_gWvP6L4t.m4a" length="45343289" type="audio/mp4"/>
